// =============================================================================
// HEADER [HEADER]
// =============================================================================

// # OmniCode Standard Library
//
// > "In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God,
// >  and the Word was God." — John 1:1
//
// The standard library provides foundational operations for OmniCode programs.
// Each module is designed around Kingdom Technology principles:
//
// - **trit**: Balanced ternary (-1, 0, +1) as the native numeric type
// - **health**: CPI-SI health tracking with Hebrew states
// - **math**: Numeric operations respecting ternary foundations
// - **io**: Input/output with witness-level awareness
// - **string**: Text operations for word processing
// - **covenant**: Covenant partnership primitives (granted/deferred/denied)

// =============================================================================
// END HEADER
// =============================================================================

// =============================================================================
// CONTEXT [CONTEXT]
// =============================================================================

// ## Design Philosophy
//
// The stdlib embodies the ternary paradigm throughout:
//
// | Binary World | Ternary World |
// |--------------|---------------|
// | true/false   | granted/deferred/denied |
// | success/fail | +1/0/-1       |
// | on/off       | positive/neutral/negative |
//
// Every operation has three possible outcomes, reflecting reality more
// accurately than binary systems.
//
// ## Module Dependencies
//
// ```
// covenant ← foundation (no dependencies)
// trit ← depends on covenant
// health ← depends on trit, covenant
// math ← depends on trit
// io ← depends on string, covenant
// string ← depends on trit
// ```

// =============================================================================
// END CONTEXT
// =============================================================================

// =============================================================================
// CONTENT [CONTENT]
// =============================================================================

// ## Modules
//
// ### trit — Balanced Ternary
// Core numeric type. All numbers are balanced ternary internally.
// Operations: negate, compare, balance, sign extraction.
//
// ### health — CPI-SI Health System
// Tracks instance health from -100 to +100 with Hebrew state mapping:
// - shavar (broken): -100 to -67
// - chaser (lacking): -66 to -34
// - ratsah (wanting): -33 to -1
// - yashar (even): 0
// - tamim (sound): +1 to +33
// - shalem (whole): +34 to +66
// - tov (good): +67 to +100
//
// ### math — Numeric Operations
// Addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, modulo.
// Trit-aware comparisons and bounds checking.
//
// ### io — Input/Output
// Display, witness, read operations.
// Witness levels: error (-1), info (0), debug (+1).
//
// ### string — Text Operations
// Length, concatenation, substring, comparison.
// Word-based processing reflecting OmniCode's sentence syntax.
//
// ### covenant — Partnership Primitives
// The foundational types: granted (+1), deferred (0), denied (-1).
// Covenant operations for decision-making and state transitions.

// =============================================================================
// END CONTENT
// =============================================================================

